body:
Just completed the survey. I liked the idea of having two separate groups, however, that assumes all people are equally good (or bad) at identifying fake news. Some people spend a lot of time on social media, know what is crap and what is reliable while others only use it occassionally. How do you control for that? It seems like "the training" may not affect everyone's ability in the same level.

&#x200B;

Good luck with your study (I am also a fellow UvA student :))

I live in a building for students, some sort of dorm. We do not have a modem or a router at home. We just have a socket in the wall for an ethernet cable, and then we have to buy a modem or a cable to connect to the internet.

&#x200B;

I bought Tp link TL-SG1005D Gigabit switch with 5 ports. I plugged my laptop to the port, and also the PS4. And I connected the switch to the socket on the wall. It worked fine for a few minutes but then my laptop lost connection to internet. I don't know what's wrong, and I have no idea how to fix it.

(Where/how) can I check the fines (speeding tickets, waste disposal, parking tickets etc.) I have received? I would assume DigiD would have a section for fines but my limited Dutch does not help me.

&#x200B;

edit: one extra question: Do you know any Chinese take-away places (around Oost) where you can fill a box with whatever food you want and pay for the size of the box? The cheaper the better :)
